OJS 3.6.0 Release Notes
Git tag: 3_6_0-0

Release date: 
============================

Configuration Changes
---------------------

See config.TEMPLATE.inc.php for a description and examples of all supported
configuration parameters.

New config.inc.php parameters added for [search]:
    - driver (default value: 'database'): Specifies which Laravel Scout driver should be used for the search engine. See config.TEMPLATE.inc.php for details on supported drivers and configuration.

New config.inc.php section for logging named logs is added, with the following parameters:
    - log_channel (default value: daily): The default logging channel. One of stack, single, daily, stderr, syslog, errorlog or null.
    - log_level (default value: debug): The minimum log level to record (debug, info, notice, warning, error, critical, alert or emergency).
    - log_stacks (default value: daily): The channels the 'stack' channel fans out to (comma-separated). Only used when log_channel = stack.
    - log_daily_days (default value: 30): The number of daily log files to retain before rotation deletes the oldest. Only applies to the 'daily' channel.
    - log_formatter (default value: unset): The Monolog formatter class for the file/stream channels. Leave unset for the default human-readable line format.
    - log_audit (default value: Off): Enable application-level security audit logging (authentication events, privilege and configuration changes, plugin lifecycle, etc.).

The following config.inc.php parameters have been removed from [schedule]:
    - task_runner: The built-in web based scheduled task runner has been removed. Scheduled tasks are now only run by lib/pkp/tools/scheduler.php, which must be run every minute by the operating system's task scheduler (e.g. cron). Installations that relied on the built-in task runner, which was enabled by default, must set this up, otherwise no scheduled task will run. See the [schedule] section of config.TEMPLATE.inc.php.
    - task_runner_interval: It only applied to the built-in task runner and is no longer used.


